WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.800
Part 2. You will hear a woman giving advice on a podcast about how to become a make-up artist

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:17.840
in the film industry. First, you have some time to look at questions 11 to 16.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:16.400
Now, listen carefully and answer questions 11 to 16.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:22.839
Hello and welcome to the Filmmaking Podcast. In this week's episode, Claire Lamar talks

00:01:22.839 --> 00:01:27.879
to us about how to become a make-up artist. Claire has been working as a make-up artist

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:34.000
in the film industry for over 20 years and has lots of useful advice about how to get

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.000
started.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:41.400
Thanks, Ian. Well, before you can become a make-up artist on films, you have to spend

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:48.199
about two years working as a make-up trainee. A good place to get your first job would be

00:01:48.199 --> 00:01:54.120
on a low-budget short film. Of course, this means that you'll be working for free, but

00:01:54.120 --> 00:02:00.080
it's often worth it for the experience. Make sure your transport costs are covered, and

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:08.559
remember, there's very unlikely to be any catering provided, so bring plenty of food.

00:02:08.559 --> 00:02:13.679
If you're lucky, you might start out on a big-budget film, where you'll get the most

00:02:13.679 --> 00:02:21.679
useful experience. On productions like this, make-up and hair styling are separate departments,

00:02:21.679 --> 00:02:26.839
so you won't need to bring your curling tongs. But you're likely to get the opportunity

00:02:26.839 --> 00:02:33.360
to work with a range of age groups, as well as different ethnicities. Doing make-up for

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.960
special effects is highly specialized, so don't expect to be offered any practical

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.919
experience in that.

00:02:41.919 --> 00:02:47.320
One problem with working in the make-up department is that it's a high-pressure environment.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:54.080
There are very few times when you'll be bored or have nothing to do. It can be stressful,

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.639
but you'll see that the top make-up artists are very professional, even when they're

00:02:58.639 --> 00:03:05.399
having to work with directors who are impatient or unhappy with the make-up artist's work.

00:03:05.399 --> 00:03:11.199
Follow your supervisor's lead, and try to remain calm at all times.

00:03:11.199 --> 00:03:16.720
I have worked with many very famous actors over the years. At first, I found it overwhelming

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:23.240
and could hardly speak. I was so in awe. That's preferable, by the way, to becoming

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:31.080
too excited and asking for selfies. Now, meeting the talent is just a normal part of the job,

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.720
and to be honest, most actors don't look that special without all the make-up.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.440
Every make-up trainee will need a make-up kit, which they'll be expected to have with

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:47.679
them at all times. Just the essentials will do for the kinds of tasks you'll be given.

00:03:47.679 --> 00:03:52.320
It won't be anything complicated. It's worth looking at what the other make-up artists

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:59.960
have in their kits, but whatever you do, don't borrow anything without asking first.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:05.279
It's very important to build your portfolio. You should take photos of all the work you

00:04:05.279 --> 00:04:12.080
do, and ideally show the different stages of make-up application if you can. But remember,

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.399
you'll need to get approval from the make-up designer in charge of the department. As you'll

00:04:17.399 --> 00:04:26.000
be sending your portfolio digitally, you won't need to get photos printed.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:33.200
Before you hear the rest of the podcast, you have some time to look at questions 17-20.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:16.440
So, what does a make-up trainee actually do? You need to think about whether you're

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:22.160
the right kind of person to do the job, and whether you'd enjoy it. So, to give you

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:28.679
some idea, here are some of the things you might be required to do. You may be asked

00:05:28.679 --> 00:05:34.600
to help prep an actor ready for make-up. Some actors will arrive having already cleansed

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:40.839
and moisturized their skin. But sometimes, you'll need to step in and get this done

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:48.040
without wasting any time. Otherwise, the make-up artist will get behind schedule.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:56.799
role in continuity. It will be your responsibility to take photos, log them digitally, and print

00:05:56.799 --> 00:06:02.839
out a hard copy to put in each actor's file. This information needs to be kept in good

00:06:02.839 --> 00:06:10.959
order as a reshoot can mean replicating make-up months later. General duties mean doing anything

00:06:10.959 --> 00:06:17.440
from getting the teas and coffees to putting on a wash. Having a positive attitude and

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:21.880
being willing to do whatever is asked of you will help you get your next film job.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:29.320
You won't be asked to apply make-up to any of the principal cast, only the extras. If there

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:34.519
are dozens of extras involved, you'll need to keep up a swift pace and not spend too

00:06:34.519 --> 00:06:39.200
long on each person. It takes quite a lot of confidence to be able to do this well.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:43.480
Okay, now about terms and conditions.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:54.920
That is the end of part two. You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to part two.

